# Acknowledged findings for the image mirrored to vendor/argocd, and only
# for it — the vendor workflow passes this file to the CRITICAL gate when a
# file matching the destination path exists. Every entry is one reviewed
# decision, and the review dies with the pin: bumping the source digest in
# vendored-images.txt is the moment to re-scan and re-justify or delete
# each line, because an acknowledgment written for one build silently
# covering the next is how a suppression file becomes a blindfold.
#
# CVE-2025-68121 — crypto/tls: incorrect certificate validation during TLS
# session resumption. Present in two binaries Argo CD v3.5.2 bundles, not
# in argocd itself: git-lfs (Go 1.25.3) and kustomize (Go 1.24.0), both
# awaiting upstream rebuilds on a fixed Go. The vulnerable path is a TLS
# *client* resuming a session against a server that can manipulate the
# handshake, and neither binary makes such a connection in this install:
# git-lfs is never invoked (the platform repository has no LFS objects, and
# the repo server fetches over HTTPS as plain git), and kustomize renders
# only content already fetched into the repo server's local checkout —
# remote bases and remote resources are not used. Revisit at the next
# argocd digest bump; if upstream has rebuilt git-lfs and kustomize on
# patched Go, this file should shrink to its header.
CVE-2025-68121
